1. Create a new HTML document and save it as `index.html`.
2. In the head section of your HTML document, add a title and style tags.
3. Inside the style tags, define styles for the container element (`#img-container`) and the image and caption inside it.
4. In the body section, create a div with the `id` of `img-container`, containing both the image tag with an `alt` attribute and the caption tag inside it.
5. Make the image a hyperlink by wrapping it in an anchor tag (`a`) and specifying the URL you want to link to.
6. Save the file and open it in a web browser to see your image with a caption and the ability to click on it to navigate to another webpage.

Here's the complete HTML and CSS code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
