The `isAlive` method checks whether the Redis connection is alive by calling the `ping()` method and returning `null` if there's no response from Redis.

The `get`, `set`, and `del` methods are all asynchronous functions that take a string `key` as an argument and perform their respective operations on the Redis server. The `set` method also accepts an optional `duration` argument which specifies the time-to-live (TTL) for the key in seconds.

Finally, we create and export an instance of `RedisClient` called `redisClient`. This instance can be imported and used throughout your application to interact with Redis.

